    "id": "l1_fpc5_ratehalf_m4_t3_misaligned_common_pencil_emptiness",
    "title": "Misaligned common-pencil three-petal LS6 atoms fail exactness",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "If the three touched petal locators are L_i=P-z_i but their source labels are not affine in z_i, then Etilde=A(P-z_0) with A nonzero. Writing D Etilde=L_2L_3 Q+V and s=ell-a, reduction modulo P-z_0 forces V=-(z_0-z_2)(z_0-z_3)Q, while cancellation gives A D=Q(P+z_0-z_2-z_3). Degree comparison gives deg Q=s>0, so Q divides both D and V and violates the LS6 gcd guard. Together with the aligned sibling, every common-pencil three-petal atom is empty.",
